\0
The loss of Gunawan left Freedom Guard forces in disarray, and several of their  allies in the rim sectors were overcome by the Imperium. Only Perlen, Strata and a few minor worlds under Freedom Guard control remain untouched. Radec was injured in the siege of Indra and was treated at a field hospital on Elmaean while second in command, Gerhad Bantrill, and what remained of the Freedom Guard Synod attempted to regroup their forces on Elmaean. However, the Imperium followed on their heels in an attempt to deal them a death blow.
\1
Radec and what remains of the Synod are attempting to regroup on Elmaean, but an Imperium invasion has landed on the planet. Engage the enemy and hold their advance. We must have time to re-establish ourselves. The Imperium is shelling our defenses. Move your base and re-establish it in a better position, then drive the Imperium from the planet.
\n\n
\cOBJECTIVES\n
\n
-->  Relocate your base to a safer location\n
-->  Protect Commander Radec \n
-->  Regroup and destroy all Imperium forces
\2
You are nearly ready. One more test awaits you.\n
\n
\cHISTORICAL OUTCOME:\n
In the dense jungles of Elmaean, Freedom Guard forces were able to use guerrilla tactics to outmaneuver the Imperium’s swarm assaults. The Freedom Guard inflicted a four to one kill ratio on the enemy and crippled the Imperium's largest ground armor division. Freedom Guard forces, scattered after the fall of Indra, were able to regroup and hold Elmaean. 
\3
You are not ready. I fear you never will be.

